import Foundation

struct GuideSection: Identifiable { let id = UUID(); let title: String; let body: String }
struct Release: Identifiable { let id = UUID(); let version: String; let date: String; let items: [String] }
/// What is drawn next to a sign's meaning.
enum SignKind { case markSport, markTick, markMoon, markGrey, pillToDo, tickDone, wordMissed, bodyCard, todayLine, yesterdayLine, green, blue, purple, weekBar, buttonFull }
struct GuideSign: Identifiable { let id = UUID(); let kind: SignKind; let name: String; let meaning: String }

enum Guide {
    static let howItWorks: [GuideSection] = [
        GuideSection(title: "What this app is for", body: "AMS Triathlon Training runs on the Mac as an iPad app, and an iPad app cannot put anything in the menu bar. AMS Tria Menu does that part. It is a separate, tiny app that shows today's training and your Body Battery at a glance.\n\nIt lives in the menu bar at the top of the screen and has no Dock icon. It only reads. It never changes your plan."),
        GuideSection(title: "The menu bar", body: "You see a small hand-drawn mark and a number. The number is always your Body Battery, from 0 to 100. A dash means it is not known.\n\nThe mark has four faces:\nA session is still to do: that sport's mark, in the sport's own colour. With several sessions, it is the first one still to do.\nNothing is left to do and at least one session is done: a green tick.\nRest day, or nothing planned: a moon.\nGrey: there is no note for today yet (a grey medal, the app's own mark), or today's session was missed (that sport's mark, in grey). Grey is never red.\n\nRest the pointer on the mark and it says the sessions and your Body Battery in words. A click opens the panel.\n\nA right click (or a control-click) shows a short menu: \"Open Triathlon\", \"Refresh now\" and \"Settings\u{2026}\"."),
        GuideSection(title: "The panel", body: "At the top are the small app tile (a white medal on green), the name, the version and the gear button for Settings.\n\nBelow it come, from top to bottom: Today, Tomorrow, This week and the Body Battery card. At the bottom is one green button, \"Open Triathlon\", which brings the Triathlon app to the front.\n\nThe panel opens under the mark and is 300 wide."),
        GuideSection(title: "Today's sessions", body: "The green heading says the day, for example \"Today \u{00B7} Tue 1 Dec\". Under it is one row for each session.\n\nA row shows the sport's mark, then the sport with its length right beside it, for example \"Run 45 min\". At the right end is a small filled pill \"to do\" in the sport's colour, or a green tick with \"done\", or the grey word \"missed\". Under that, in small grey words, stands the session's title.\n\nA click on a row opens that session in AMS Triathlon Training. The grey line under the rows says so.\n\nOn a rest day there is one row with the moon and \"Rest day\".\n\nIf there is no note for today, grey words say why. For example: \"No note for today yet. Triathlon writes it when it opens.\", or that Triathlon is not on this Mac, or that the Mac did not let the app read the note."),
        GuideSection(title: "Tomorrow and this week", body: "\"Tomorrow\" has a blue heading. It names tomorrow's first session, for example \"Bike, 1 h 10 min\", or \"Rest day\". It is missing when nothing is planned.\n\n\"This week\" has a purple heading. It says, for example, \"40 min done of 3 h 35 min planned\". Under it a slim purple bar is filled to that share."),
        GuideSection(title: "Body Battery", body: "The raspberry card has white words. It shows \"Body Battery\", the number large, and small words such as \"watch synced 15:09\". That is when your watch last sent its readings. When it was not today, the weekday stands in front of the time.\n\nUnder it is a small curve of today. A white line has a dot at the newest reading. Yesterday is a thin dark plum line with the word \"yesterday\". The curve runs from midnight to midnight.\n\nThe curve is only as fine as the watch's syncs. The watch sends its readings a few times a day, so the line has few corners."),
        GuideSection(title: "Where the figures come from", body: "Today's sessions, tomorrow and the week come from a small note that AMS Triathlon Training (2.8 or newer) writes on this Mac. It writes it each time it opens and when the plan changes. AMS Tria Menu reads the note once a minute.\n\nThe note counts only for its own day, so you never see yesterday's session. A note older than 36 hours is not used either.\n\nBody Battery comes from your own AMS Garmin Bridge Board, running on this Mac. They are the same numbers the Board shows. The app asks it every 30 minutes, and when the panel opens if the last answer is more than 5 minutes old. It asks so rarely because each answer makes the Board ask Garmin a good dozen questions, and Body Battery only changes when the watch syncs. No Garmin key is kept in this app.\n\nIf the Board does not answer, the app shows Body Battery as AMS Triathlon Training last read it, with the small words \"as Triathlon last read it\". If neither is there, you see a dash and \"Garmin Board not answering\".\n\nEarly in the day the Board may answer but have nothing for today yet, because the watch has not synced. Then you see a dash and \"no reading yet today\". The app never shows yesterday's number as today's.\n\nYesterday's line is the one AMS Triathlon Training read (the same line as on its Body page). If that is missing, the app uses its own memory of yesterday. It keeps the last three days' curves on this Mac only.\n\nNothing leaves the Mac. The app never contacts Garmin or the internet."),
        GuideSection(title: "Open Triathlon quietly", body: "Triathlon writes today's note only when it opens. So the app can open Triathlon for you, in the background: hidden, never in front, with no window. The note is there a few seconds later.\n\nIt does this when there is no note for today, which is each morning or after midnight. While a session is still to do, it does it again every 30 minutes. If Triathlon is still running hidden, it is closed politely and opened hidden again, so it reads the plan afresh. That way a session you log on the iPhone turns into the green tick here.\n\nWhen everything is done, or it is a rest day, the app leaves Triathlon alone. It never touches Triathlon while its window is showing.\n\nIf a try brings no note, the app waits 20 minutes before the next.\n\nThe switch is in Settings and is on at first. With it off, the grey mark and the words \"No note for today yet\" stay until you open Triathlon yourself. \"Refresh now\" in the right-click menu still works.\n\nOn the Mac, Triathlon cannot log a session. Only the iPhone logs. So there is no \"done\" button here. A click only opens the session."),
        GuideSection(title: "First start", body: "Nothing to set up. The app starts reading as soon as it runs. \"Open at login\" is switched on in Settings when the app is installed.\n\nOn this Mac the app read Triathlon's note without any question, because both apps are yours. Should the Mac ever ask whether \"AMS Tria Menu\" may access data from other apps, answer Allow. If it was refused, the panel says so, and you can allow it in System Settings, under Privacy & Security."),
        GuideSection(title: "Settings", body: "Open Settings with the gear button in the panel. It has three tabs: \"Settings\", \"How it works\" and \"What's new\". At the bottom of every tab are the version, \"Quit AMS Tria Menu\" and the green \"Done\" button. The Escape key also closes the window.\n\nThe \"Settings\" tab has \"Open at login\". While it is on, the app also comes back by itself if it ever stops unexpectedly. The Mac's own login list only starts the app at login. A second helper order, the keeper, also starts it again after an unexpected stop. It does not do that after Quit.\n\nIt has \"Open Triathlon quietly\", with two lines that say what it does.\n\nIt has a section \"Where the figures come from\" with two lines. The first says when Triathlon wrote today's note. The second says that Body Battery comes from the Garmin Board, and when the watch last synced.\n\nOnly one copy of the app runs. The copy that started first stays."),
        GuideSection(title: "A place in sight", body: "A new menu bar item can land behind the notch when the bar is full. So the app picks a place in sight when it starts for the first time.\n\nIf the Mac ever pushes the mark out of sight, to the far left, the app puts it back after 10 seconds."),
        GuideSection(title: "Good to know: the limits", body: "The app only knows what AMS Triathlon Training has written down and what the Garmin Board says. It cannot see your watch itself.\n\nBody Battery is only as fresh as your watch's last sync. The curve has a corner for each reading, so a few readings a day make a simple line.\n\nThere is no \"done\" button on the Mac. Only the iPhone logs a session.\n\nThere are no notifications and no large graph window in this first version.\n\nThe app needs AMS Triathlon Training 2.8 or newer on this Mac, and the AMS Garmin Bridge Board for Body Battery."),
    ]

    static let signs: [GuideSign] = [
        GuideSign(kind: .markSport, name: "A sport's mark in its colour", meaning: "A session of that sport is still to do. Swim blue, bike yellow, run green, strength orange, rowing teal, mobility purple, race red."),
        GuideSign(kind: .markTick, name: "Green tick in the menu bar", meaning: "Everything for today is done."),
        GuideSign(kind: .markMoon, name: "Moon", meaning: "Rest day, or nothing planned."),
        GuideSign(kind: .markGrey, name: "Grey mark", meaning: "No note for today yet, or the session was missed."),
        GuideSign(kind: .pillToDo, name: "Filled pill \"to do\"", meaning: "This session is still to do. The pill has the sport's colour."),
        GuideSign(kind: .tickDone, name: "Tick with \"done\"", meaning: "This session is done. Nothing else is ever a tick."),
        GuideSign(kind: .wordMissed, name: "Grey \"missed\"", meaning: "This session was planned for today and not done."),
        GuideSign(kind: .bodyCard, name: "Raspberry card", meaning: "Body Battery."),
        GuideSign(kind: .todayLine, name: "White line with a dot", meaning: "Today's Body Battery so far. The dot is the newest reading."),
        GuideSign(kind: .yesterdayLine, name: "Thin dark line", meaning: "Yesterday's Body Battery."),
        GuideSign(kind: .green, name: "Green heading", meaning: "Today."),
        GuideSign(kind: .blue, name: "Blue heading", meaning: "Tomorrow."),
        GuideSign(kind: .purple, name: "Purple heading", meaning: "This week."),
        GuideSign(kind: .weekBar, name: "Slim purple bar", meaning: "How much of the week's planned time is done."),
        GuideSign(kind: .buttonFull, name: "A button in full colour", meaning: "The main thing to do on that screen."),
    ]

    static let whatsNew: [Release] = [
        Release(version: "0.1", date: "26 Nov 2026", items: [
            "New app: AMS Tria Menu, a small Mac menu bar app with no Dock icon. It shows today's training and your Body Battery at a glance. It only reads and never changes your plan.",
            "The menu bar shows a small hand-drawn mark and a number. The number is always your Body Battery, from 0 to 100, or a dash when it is not known.",
            "The mark is the sport's mark in the sport's colour while a session is still to do: swim blue, bike yellow, run green, strength orange, rowing teal, mobility purple, race red. With several sessions it is the first one still to do.",
            "The mark is a green tick when nothing is left to do and at least one session is done. It is a slate grey moon on a rest day or when nothing is planned. It is grey when there is no note for today yet, or when today's session was missed. Grey is never red.",
            "Rest the pointer on the mark and it says the sessions and your Body Battery in words. A click opens the panel. A right click (or control-click) gives a short menu: \"Open Triathlon\", \"Refresh now\" and \"Settings\u{2026}\".",
            "The panel shows Today with one row for each session: the sport's mark, the sport with its length (\"Run 45 min\"), a filled \"to do\" pill, a green tick with \"done\" or a grey \"missed\", and the session's title in small grey words. A click on a row opens that session in AMS Triathlon Training.",
            "The panel also shows Tomorrow (the first session, or \"Rest day\") and This week (for example \"40 min done of 3 h 35 min planned\", with a slim purple bar).",
            "The raspberry Body Battery card shows the number large, when the watch last synced, and a small curve from midnight to midnight: today as a white line with a dot at the newest reading, and yesterday as a thin dark line.",
            "Today's sessions come from a small note that AMS Triathlon Training 2.8 or newer writes on this Mac. The app reads it once a minute. It shows only a note for today, and none older than 36 hours.",
            "Body Battery comes from your AMS Garmin Bridge Board on this Mac, every 30 minutes and when the panel opens. If the Board does not answer, the app shows it as Triathlon last read it, or a dash with \"Garmin Board not answering\". Before the watch's first sync of the day it shows a dash with \"no reading yet today\", never yesterday's number. No Garmin key is stored here, and nothing leaves the Mac.",
            "\"Open Triathlon quietly\" is a switch in Settings, on at first. When there is no note for today, the app opens Triathlon hidden in the background, never in front. While a session is still to do it does so again every 30 minutes, so a session logged on the iPhone turns into the green tick. It never touches Triathlon while its window is showing, and waits 20 minutes after a try that brought no note.",
            "The sport marks are AMS Triathlon Training's own hand-drawn marks from the central icon library, so they look the same in both apps.",
            "Settings has three tabs: \"Settings\", \"How it works\" and \"What's new\". It has \"Open at login\" with the keeper that brings the app back if it ever stops unexpectedly, the quiet-opening switch, and two lines that say where the figures come from. The version, \"Quit AMS Tria Menu\" and a green \"Done\" button are at the bottom of every tab.",
            "The app picks a place in the menu bar that is in sight at first start, and puts itself back if the Mac pushes it out of sight. Only one copy of the app runs.",
        ]),
    ]
}
